Package: froxlor
Version: 2.3.16-dev
Section: web
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Froxlor Team <info@froxlor.org>
Depends: php (>= 7.4), php-cli, php-common, php-curl, php-fileinfo, php-filter, php-gd, php-gmp, php-json, php-mbstring, php-mysql, php-openssl, php-pdo, php-posix, php-session, php-simplexml, php-sockets, php-tokenizer, php-xml, php-zip, apache2 | nginx, mysql-server | mariadb-server, wget
Recommends: cron, logrotate
Description: Froxlor - PHP-based hosting control panel
 Froxlor is a server administration software for your needs. Developed by
 experienced server administrators, this panel simplifies the effort of
 managing your hosting panel.
 .
 This package provides the Froxlor panel files under /usr/share/froxlor.
 On first installation, run the web-based installer or copy
 lib/userdata.inc.php.dist to lib/userdata.inc.php and configure your
 database credentials, then call admin_updates.php to initialize the schema.
 .
 On upgrade, the database update chain is executed automatically via
 admin_updates.php (CLI). Make sure your MySQL/MariaDB server is running
 and reachable before upgrading.
Homepage: https://froxlor.org/
